Build the novadeck_radiomac module.

Same mechanism as 0003: a stanza in grub-core/Makefile.core.def, with the
generated module tables regenerated by boot/grub.sh's ./autogen.sh.

`enable = arm64_efi` rather than `efi` like novadeck: the module needs both
EFI (the chip-info protocol) and the EFI fdt loader, and arm64-efi is the only
target we build.

diff --git a/grub-core/Makefile.core.def b/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
index 80a4c0f..93cae9d 100644
--- a/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
+++ b/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
@@ -848,6 +848,12 @@ module = {
   enable = efi;
 };
 
+module = {
+  name = novadeck_radiomac;
+  common = commands/efi/novadeck_radiomac.c;
+  enable = arm64_efi;
+};
+
 module = {
   name = efitextmode;
   efi = commands/efi/efitextmode.c;
